\subsection{Ranking an Item in Several Places}%
\label{sec:place-in-places}

An item with several parents is ranked in each of its places by the
same helper, so that [[add]], [[edit]] and [[rm]] agree on the order in
which places are asked and on which of them wins
(\cref{sec:ranking-context}).  The places are taken from the highest
down.  The top level comes first, since it has no upper bound and so
can give the highest number of all; then the parents in the order of
their own numbers, since a place under a higher parent can give a
higher number; a done parent comes last, as it ranks nothing that is
still open.  An unranked or missing parent offers no place to rank in
and is left out.

<<placement helpers>>=
def places_highest_first(places, by_id):
    """Return the `places` an item can be ranked in, the one
    that can give the highest number first."""
    def order(place):
        if place == ROOT_ID:
            return (0, 0.0)
        parent = by_id[place]
        return (1 if parent.status != "done" else 2, -parent.priority)
    return sorted(
        (
            place for place in places
            if place == ROOT_ID
            or (place in by_id and by_id[place].priority is not None)
        ),
        key=order,
    )
@

Visiting the places in that order lets the helper skip the questions
that cannot matter.  Once a number is found, a place whose parent ranks
at or below it can only give a lower one, since everything in its range
lies below the parent, so it is not asked.  Each place is asked through
a stand-in, a copy of the item whose only parent is that place, which
makes [[place_existing_item]] rank it among the siblings ranked there
and nowhere else.  The highest answer is the item's number, or the
number it started with if that is higher.

<<placement helpers>>=
def place_in_places(
    todos: list[TodoItem],
    item: TodoItem,
    places,
    placement: str | None = None,
    number: float | None = None,
) -> float | None:
    """Return the highest number `item` gets in any of
    `places`, or `number` if that is higher.

    `placement` is a `PLACE_*` value, or `None` to ask
    the user; places that cannot beat the number found so
    far are not asked.  `None` means no place could rank
    the item.
    """
    by_id = {t.id: t for t in todos}
    for place in places_highest_first(places, by_id):
        parent = by_id.get(place)
        if (
            number is not None and parent is not None
            and parent.priority <= number
        ):
            continue
        stand_in = copy.copy(item)
        stand_in.parents = [place]
        found = place_existing_item(todos, stand_in, placement)
        if found is not None and (number is None or found > number):
            number = found
    return number
@

