\subsubsection{Auto-activating Ancestors}

The converse of auto-completing a parent is auto-activating one.  When a
user starts a child directly ([[todo start 7]] where~7 is a sub-item of
parent~5), the parent should already be on the active stack---otherwise
the hierarchy reported by [[todo status]] would be incomplete, and
tracking would miss the parent's labels entirely.

Rather than requiring the user to manually start every ancestor first, we
walk up the line of parents and activate any ancestor that is not
already on the stack.  The line is [[context_path]] with the stack as
the context (\cref{sec:todo-parents}), so where an item has a parent
that is already active, its line runs through that one.  It comes
root first, so the outermost ancestor is pushed first, giving the
stack the correct root-to-leaf order.

Each activated ancestor is claimed by the worker whose session the
item belongs to, and gets its labels tracked in that session.  Which
ancestors are missing is decided twice: once on the snapshot, to
avoid taking the lock when nothing is missing, and again under the
lock, where an ancestor that someone else activated meanwhile is left
to them.  Only the ancestors actually pushed under the lock are
tracked; tracking the snapshot's list would start a second clock on
an ancestor that another worker's session already runs.
Without this, the parent would appear in the hierarchy but
accumulate no time---defeating the purpose of nested tracking.  We
reuse the same [[start_tracking_labels]] path that
[[<<start tracking via track module>>]] uses for the explicitly
started item.

Tmux launches need one extra rule.  When [[todo start --pane]] or
[[todo start --window]] is about to create a new tracked tmux context, the
generic current-shell tmux update would target the source pane or window
instead of the newly launched one.  We therefore thread an
[[update_tmux_context]] flag through ancestor activation so tmux launches
can mirror [[track start]] and let [[run_tmux_command()]] publish the
authoritative pane or window state.

<<helpers>>=
def ensure_ancestors_active(
    item, todos, stack, *,
    update_tmux_context=True,
):
    """Activate and track all ancestors of ``item``.

    Walks up the parent chain and, for each ancestor
    not already on the active stack, pushes it onto
    the stack and starts tracking its labels.

    Returns the list of ancestor items that were
    newly activated (outermost first).
    """
    missing = [
        ancestor
        for ancestor in context_path(todos, item, stack)
        if ancestor.id not in stack
    ]

    if not missing:
        return []

    worker = session_worker(item)

    def push_ancestors(next_id, todos, stack):
        pushed = set()
        for ancestor in missing:
            if ancestor.id not in stack:
                idx = stack.index(item.id) \
                    if item.id in stack else len(stack)
                push_active(stack, ancestor.id, idx)
                pushed.add(ancestor.id)
        for fresh in todos:
            if fresh.id in pushed:
                fresh.claimed_by = worker
                fresh.context_claim = True
        return next_id, todos, stack, pushed

    _, _, _, pushed = mutate_todo_state(push_ancestors)
    missing = [
        ancestor for ancestor in missing
        if ancestor.id in pushed
    ]

    try:
        from nytid.cli.track import (
            start_tracking_labels,
        )
        for ancestor in missing:
            labels = list(ancestor.labels) + [
                f"todo:{ancestor.id}"
            ]
            started, _, _ = start_tracking_labels(
                labels,
                start_time=datetime.datetime.now(),
                who=worker,
                update_tmux_context=update_tmux_context,
            )
            typer.echo(
                f"  Auto-started parent: "
                f"#{ancestor.id} {ancestor.title}"
            )
            if started:
                typer.echo(
                    f"  Tracking: "
                    f"{', '.join(sorted(started))}"
                )
    except ImportError:
        pass

    return missing
