\subsubsection{Releasing Context Ancestors}%
\label{sec:todo-release-context}

Activating ancestors has a converse that we owe the worker.  An
ancestor activated only as context for a child is claimed by the
child's worker (\cref{sec:todo-claim}), and nothing would ever give it
back: when an agent finishes the one child it was given, the parent
stays on the stack in the agent's name.  The user then cannot
[[stop]] it without [[--who]], cannot [[done]] it at all, and a cron
[[next --who dan-claude]] keeps descending into it, looking for the
agent's next child under a parent that was only ever context.

So when an item leaves the stack---stopped, completed, removed, or
at the end of a run---we walk up from it and look at each ancestor
that its worker claimed as context ([[context_claim]]).  If that
worker still has an active item below the ancestor, the context is
still needed and stays.  Otherwise it goes: to another worker who
has an active item below it, if any, since the ancestor is that
worker's context now; or off the stack, if nobody works below it any
more.  Tracking follows the claim: the old claimant's clock for the
ancestor stops, and a new claimant's starts.

The ancestors are the line [[context_path]] follows with the stack as
context (\cref{sec:todo-parents}): the line along which
[[ensure_ancestors_active]] activated them.  We walk from the
innermost ancestor outwards and decide each one on the stack as the
previous decisions left it, so a grandparent that
was context only for a released parent is released with it.  An
ancestor that the worker started explicitly is not touched.  That is
the nested workflow \enquote{[[start 5]], [[start 7]], [[done]],
[[done]]}, in which the parent must stay active after the child is
done, and which is why [[context_claim]] exists at all: the claimant
alone cannot tell the two apart.

The decision is made under the lock, on the stack as it is; the
tracking changes follow outside it, like every other tracking I/O
(\cref{sec:todo-read-modify-write}).

<<helpers>>=
def release_context_ancestors(item, worker):
    """Release ancestors `worker` claimed as context for `item`.

    `item` has just left the stack.  Each ancestor that
    `worker` claimed only as context, and under which
    `worker` has no active item left, is handed to the
    worker of another active item below it, or leaves the
    stack if there is none; tracking follows.  Returns the
    list of `(ancestor, new claimant or None)` changes.
    """
    if worker is None:
        return []

    def update(next_id, todos, stack):
        changes = []
        for ancestor in reversed(context_path(todos, item, stack)):
            <<decide what becomes of a context ancestor>>
        return next_id, todos, stack, changes

    _, todos, _, changes = mutate_todo_state(update)
    <<move the tracking of released context ancestors>>
    return changes
@

An ancestor is only ours to release if it is active, claimed as
context, and claimed by the worker whose item left.  The heir, if
there is one, is the worker of the latest active item below it in
stack order: the most recently started work under that ancestor.

<<decide what becomes of a context ancestor>>=
if not (
    ancestor.id in stack
    and ancestor.context_claim
    and ancestor.claimed_by == worker
):
    continue
below = [
    child for child in descendants_of(todos, ancestor.id)
    if child.id in stack
]
if any(session_worker(child) == worker for child in below):
    continue
if below:
    heir = max(below, key=lambda child: stack.index(child.id))
    ancestor.claimed_by = session_worker(heir)
    changes.append((ancestor, ancestor.claimed_by))
else:
    stack.remove(ancestor.id)
    changes.append((ancestor, None))
@

The old claimant's tracking stops by name, since the claim no longer
says it was theirs; the labels that the claimant's other active items
carry stay protected as in every stop.

<<move the tracking of released context ancestors>>=
for ancestor, heir in changes:
    stop_todo_tracking(
        ancestor.id, ancestor, todos, worker=worker,
    )
    if heir is None:
        typer.echo(
            f"  Released parent: #{ancestor.id} {ancestor.title}"
        )
        continue
    typer.echo(
        f"  Handed parent #{ancestor.id} {ancestor.title} "
        f"to {heir}"
    )
    try:
        from nytid.cli.track import start_tracking_labels
    except ImportError:
        continue
    start_tracking_labels(
        todo_track_labels(ancestor, ancestor.id),
        start_time=datetime.datetime.now(),
        who=heir,
        update_tmux_context=False,
    )
@

