When a parent is set, inherit its deadline and labels unless the user
explicitly provided overrides.  This chunk is shared by both paths of
[[add]], which makes it the single place where a command-line
[[--deadline]] becomes stored data---so it is also where that string
has to be validated.  An inherited parent deadline needs no check: it
was normalized when the parent was written.  Every parent named must
exist, and [[parent_items]] keeps them by id for the priority
resolution below.

<<inherit from parent>>=
inherited_labels = list(label) if label else []
inherited_deadline = normalize_deadline(deadline)
parent_items = {}
for parent_id in resolved_parents:
    if parent_id == ROOT_ID:
        continue
    parent_items[parent_id] = next(
        (t for t in todos if t.id == parent_id),
        None,
    )
    if parent_items[parent_id] is None:
        typer.echo(
            f"Error: parent #{parent_id} not found",
            err=True,
        )
        raise typer.Exit(1)
from_labels, from_deadline = inherit_from_parents(
    parent_items.values()
)
if not label and from_labels:
    inherited_labels = from_labels
if deadline is None and from_deadline:
    inherited_deadline = from_deadline
@

A child of several parents belongs to all of their contexts, so it
takes the union of their labels: a task shared by two courses is
tracked under both.  Of their deadlines it takes the earliest, since
the item has to be done by the time the first parent that contains it
is due.  A deadline that does not parse, which only a hand-edited
file holds, loses to any that does, and is taken only when no other is
there.  [[import]] inherits from its one parent through the same
helper, so the two commands agree on what a parent passes on.

<<helpers>>=
def inherit_from_parents(parents):
    """Return the labels and deadline a new child inherits.

    The labels are the union of the `parents`' labels and the
    deadline is the earliest of their deadlines, or `None`.
    """
    parents = list(parents)
    labels = sorted({
        label for parent in parents for label in parent.labels
    })
    deadlines = [p.deadline for p in parents if p.deadline]
    if not deadlines:
        return labels, None

    def earliest_first(deadline):
        parsed = naive_local_datetime(deadline)
        return (parsed is None, parsed or datetime.datetime.max)
    return labels, min(deadlines, key=earliest_first)
@

