Everything so far worked on the snapshot read at the start of the
command, including the binary search, which may have kept the user
answering questions for a while.  The item itself is created inside a
locked callback (\cref{sec:todo-read-modify-write}).  Its ID has to
come from the [[next_id]] that is current when the item is written:
taking it from the snapshot is what let two overlapping [[add]]s
hand out the same ID.  The parents chosen at the start are looked up
again for the same reason, each of them, since one may have been
removed in the meantime, and a child of a removed item would be
promoted to the top level by [[get_visible_roots]] instead of being
refused.  Once stored, the new item cuts short the range of the
sibling directly above it, so [[settle_placement]] compresses that
sibling's subtree in the same callback
(\cref{sec:sibling-above-squeezed}).

<<append the new todo under the lock>>=
def append_new_todo(next_id, todos, stack):
    for parent_id in parent_items:
        require_todo(todos, parent_id)
    item = TodoItem(
        id=next_id,
        title=title,
        labels=inherited_labels,
        priority=priority,
        status="pending",
        created=now,
        deadline=inherited_deadline,
        estimated=estimated_hours,
        description=description or "",
        parents=resolved_parents,
        who=resolved_who,
        wd=resolved_wd,
        worktree=normalize_worktree_name(worktree),
        env=resolved_env,
        command=run_command,
        discovered_from=resolved_discovered_from,
    )
    for paragraph in note or []:
        append_note_to_item(item, paragraph)
    todos.append(item)
    settle_placement(todos, item)
    return next_id + 1, todos, stack, item

*_, item = mutate_todo_state(append_new_todo)
@

Let's verify the squeeze from the side of [[add]]: a new top-level item
at~4.0, between A at~5.0 and B at~3.0, leaves A's children between A
and the new item, whether the item came from the flags or from the
editor.

<<test functions>>=
def a_and_b_with_children():
    """Ranked A and B at 5 and 3; A's children at 4.5
    and 3.5."""
    return [
        TodoItem(
            id=n, title=t, priority=p, parents=[parent],
            created="2026-02-20T10:00:00",
            who=default_username,
        )
        for n, t, p, parent in [
            (1, "A", 5.0, None),
            (2, "B", 3.0, None),
            (3, "A1", 4.5, 1),
            (4, "A2", 3.5, 1),
        ]
    ]


@pytest.mark.parametrize("args", [
    ["add", "-t", "New", "--prio", "4", "--top-level"],
    ["add", "--edit", "--prio", "4", "--top-level"],
])
def test_add_squeezes_the_sibling_above(
    temp_todo_dir, args,
):
