With a depth limit the walk stops there, and the hint below owes the
reader the number of rows a bare [[-r]] would add: the same walk
with the limit lifted, under the same cap and the same done filter,
less what is already on the screen.  That second walk's cap count is
not used, because the cap hint must describe the listing that was
printed, not the one that was not.
The rows carry the same notes on where else an item is as the tree of
[[ls]] (\cref{sec:todo-tree-notes}), with the viewed item as the
parent of the first level.

