\paragraph{The plain renderer}

This is the output [[view]] has always produced, and its layout is kept
rather than tidied: the first two groups of metadata share a line each
(priority, deadline and estimate; then labels and worker) and the
remaining fields get a line of their own.
[[VIEW_INLINE_FIELD_GROUPS]] records that grouping so the renderer can
reproduce it from the shared field list.
Notes go through [[print_markdown]] with the terminal form switched
off, which prints them as written under the same two-space indent as
before.

<<constants>>=
VIEW_INLINE_FIELD_GROUPS = (
    ("Priority", "Deadline", "Est"),
    ("Labels", "Worker"),
)
@

<<render view as plain text>>=
typer.echo(f"#{item.id} {item.title} [{item.status}]")
for group in VIEW_INLINE_FIELD_GROUPS:
    line = [f"{k}: {v}" for k, v in fields if k in group]
    if line:
        typer.echo("  " + "  ".join(line))
grouped = {k for group in VIEW_INLINE_FIELD_GROUPS for k in group}
for label, value in fields:
    if label not in grouped:
        typer.echo(f"  {label}: {value}")
if item.description:
    typer.echo(f"  Description: {item.description}")
<<print notes as plain text>>
<<print sub-items as plain text>>
