@

Each rule that hid something says so, in the order the rules ran:
the done filter first, then the cap that was applied to what it left.
Read the other way round the second number would not be checkable
against anything on the screen, because the cap's count already
speaks only about items the done filter had passed.

The depth limit is the third rule and its line comes last, for the
reason the cap's comes after the done filter's: its number is the
rows [[-r]] would add to the listing as it stands, cap and done
filter included, so a reader can check it by adding the flag and
counting.

Let's verify the default: the children are listed and the deeper
levels counted, in both renderers, the count is what [[-r]] then
adds, a parent of leaves says nothing, and [[-r 0]] is the default
depth again.

<<test functions>>=
def test_view_default_lists_children_only(temp_todo_dir):
    """Without -r the children are listed; deeper levels counted."""
    save_todos(5, [
        TodoItem(
            id=1, title="Parent task",
            created="2026-02-20T10:00:00",
        ),
        TodoItem(
            id=2, title="Child task", parents=[1],
            created="2026-02-20T10:00:00",
        ),
        TodoItem(
            id=3, title="Grandchild task", parents=[2],
            created="2026-02-20T10:00:00",
        ),
        TodoItem(
            id=4, title="Leaf child", parents=[1],
            created="2026-02-20T10:00:00",
        ),
    ])
    hint = "(1 deeper sub-items hidden, use --recursive to list)"

    plain = runner.invoke(cli, ["view", "1"])
    assert plain.exit_code == 0
    assert "Child task" in plain.stdout
    assert "Leaf child" in plain.stdout
    assert "Grandchild task" not in plain.stdout
    assert hint in plain.stdout

    rich = runner.invoke(cli, ["view", "1", "--format", "rich"])
    assert rich.exit_code == 0
    assert "Child task" in rich.stdout
    assert "Grandchild task" not in rich.stdout
    assert hint in rich.stdout

    listed = runner.invoke(cli, ["view", "1", "-r"])
    assert listed.exit_code == 0
    assert "Grandchild task" in listed.stdout
    assert "hidden" not in listed.stdout

    explicit = runner.invoke(cli, ["view", "1", "-r", "0"])
    assert "Child task" in explicit.stdout
    assert "Grandchild task" not in explicit.stdout

    leaves = runner.invoke(cli, ["view", "2"])
    assert leaves.exit_code == 0
    assert "Grandchild task" in leaves.stdout
    assert "hidden" not in leaves.stdout


