Without the table the sub-item line has to carry the columns itself,
so it is assembled in the same order and colours the header row would
have given them.
The blocks below it are rendered rather than printed verbatim---this
renderer was chosen precisely for that---and both line and blocks are
padded by depth, which is what replaces the table's indented title
column.

<<print each sub-item with its blocks>>=
for (depth, child), place in zip(rows, row_places):
    mark = VIEW_STATUS_MARKS.get(child.status, child.status)
    console.print(Padding(
        Text.assemble(
            (f"#{child.id} ", "cyan"),
            (f"[{mark}] ",
             VIEW_STATUS_STYLES.get(child.status, "")),
            child.title,
            (f" {place}" if place else "", "dim"),
        ),
        (0, 0, 0, 2 + 2 * depth),
    ))
    if child.description:
        print_markdown(
            child.description, indent=4 + 2 * depth,
            terminal=True,
        )
    if child.notes:
        print_markdown(
            child.notes, indent=4 + 2 * depth,
            terminal=True,
        )
