Labels accept three flags whose interaction we resolved earlier:
[[--label]] replaces, [[--add-label]]/[[--remove-label]] adjust relative to
the current set.  We reject the contradictory [[-l]]-with-[[-a]]/[[-r]]
combination before touching anything, delegate the relative merge to
[[apply_label_edits]], and translate its [[ValueError]] (same label added
and removed) into a non-zero exit.  No-op warnings from the helper are
echoed to stderr but do not fail the command:

<<apply label edits>>=
if label is not None and (add_label or remove_label):
    typer.echo(
        "Error: --label cannot be combined with "
        "--add-label/--remove-label",
        err=True,
    )
    raise typer.Exit(1)
if label is not None:
    item.labels = list(label)
elif add_label or remove_label:
    try:
        new_labels, warnings = apply_label_edits(
            item.labels, add_label or [], remove_label or [],
        )
    except ValueError as exc:
        typer.echo(f"Error: {exc}", err=True)
        raise typer.Exit(1)
    for warning in warnings:
        typer.echo(f"Warning: {warning}", err=True)
    item.labels = new_labels
