A number given with [[--prio]] has to fit one of the item's places,
whichever way the places are given: B is under A at~5.0 and D at~3.0,
or gains D in the same command, and~4.6, in A's range, and~2.5, in
D's, both fit, while~10 fits neither.  A number that fits only the
lower place is still subject to the rule: B at~2.5 lies below A's
range, so it is lifted to the bottom of it, $(3.0 + 5.0) / 2$; and E,
D's child, given A with~2.5, which fits D, ends at the bottom of A's
range too, below B, at~$(3.0 + 4.5) / 2$.

