[[--discovered-from]] sets the provenance link
(\cref{sec:todo-discovered-from}) after the fact.  The need is the one
[[--parent]] meets: an item added at the top level before the link
existed, or added with [[--no-discovered-from]], or added from a pane
in which a different todo was active.  [[0]] clears the link, for the
reason it promotes an item with [[--parent]]: no todo has that ID, so
it can only mean \enquote{none}.

A positive ID must name an existing todo other than the item itself.
The existence check is [[add]]'s and, as there, it runs on the
snapshot only: a source removed before the commit leaves a link that
[[view]] shows as removed, which is no worse than removing it a moment
later.  An item cannot have been discovered while working on itself,
so that link is refused rather than stored.  The new value reaches
the store through the replay in
[[<<commit the flag edits under the lock>>]], like every other field
this path sets, so a concurrent change to any other field survives.

<<argument and option definitions>>=
edit_discovered_from_opt = typer.Option(
    "--discovered-from",
    help="ID of the todo this one was found while working on "
         "(0 = none)",
    autocompletion=complete_todo_ids)
<<set the edited item's [[discovered_from]]>>=
if discovered_from == 0:
    item.discovered_from = None
elif discovered_from is not None:
    if discovered_from == item.id:
        typer.echo(
            f"Error: #{item.id} cannot be discovered from "
            "itself",
            err=True,
        )
        raise typer.Exit(1)
    check_discovered_from(todos, discovered_from, False)
    item.discovered_from = discovered_from
