\subsection{Testing the [[--parent]] Flag}

Reparenting addresses the common accident of creating a todo as a
child of an active item when a top-level item was intended.  We
verify both directions: promoting a child to the top level and
moving it under a different parent.  Both re-rank as part of the
move, which the first test meets as a binary-search question and the
second as a silent placement in the new parent's still-empty child
range.  Neither parent in the second test was given a priority, so
both hold the constructor default
(\cref{sec:ranked-and-unranked}) and that range is the unit-wide
fallback below them (\cref{sec:child-priority-helpers}).  An item in
two places, the top level and under~A, is moved under~B, and the
command names both places it left.  We also confirm that supplying an
invalid parent ID is rejected with a non-zero exit code rather than
silently storing a dangling reference.

<<test functions>>=
def test_edit_reparent_toplevel(temp_todo_dir):
    """--parent 0 promotes a child to top-level."""
    save_todos(3, [
        TodoItem(
            id=1, title="Parent",
            created="2026-02-20T10:00:00",
        ),
        TodoItem(
            id=2, title="Child", parents=[1],
            priority=0.5,
