The two options that name a neighbour take an ID, and completing that
ID from the existing todos is what makes them usable by hand as well as
from a script.

<<argument and option definitions>>=
above_opt = typer.Option(
    "--above",
    help="Place just above sibling ID",
    autocompletion=complete_todo_ids)
below_opt = typer.Option(
    "--below",
    help="Place just below sibling ID",
    autocompletion=complete_todo_ids)
@

The flags are mutually exclusive, and all four need to know which item
they are placing.  Without an ID the command means \enquote{rank
everything that is unranked}, and a single placement cannot describe
what should happen to a whole batch: applying [[--top]] to each item in
turn would leave them stacked in visiting order, which is not what the
flag says.  We refuse rather than invent an interpretation.

<<validate reprioritize placement>>=
reject_conflicting_flags({
    "--top": top,
    "--bottom": bottom,
    "--above": above is not None,
    "--below": below is not None,
})
places = (
    top or bottom
    or above is not None
    or below is not None
)
if todo_id is None and places:
    typer.echo(
        "Error: --top, --bottom, --above and --below "
        "need a todo ID",
        err=True,
    )
    raise typer.Exit(1)
@

Turning the flags into a placement is a small dispatch; the work is in
validating what [[--above]] and [[--below]] point at.

<<resolve the reprioritize placement>>=
placement = None
target = None
ranked_as = item
if top:
    placement = PLACE_TOP
elif bottom:
    placement = PLACE_BOTTOM
elif above is not None or below is not None:
    if above is not None:
        placement = PLACE_ABOVE
        target_id = above
    else:
        placement = PLACE_BELOW
        target_id = below
    <<resolve the placement target>>
@

A target has to be an item this one can actually be ranked against,
and each way of failing that has its own remedy, so each gets its own
message rather than one generic refusal.  An item is not its own
neighbour; an item under a different parent is in a different ordering
entirely, and so is a shared item ranked under another of its parents
(\cref{sec:ranking-context}); and an unranked target has no number to
sit next to, which
the user fixes by ranking it first.

\paragraph{A neighbour in another place.}%
\label{sec:reprioritize-in-a-place}
An item with several parents has siblings in each place, and a
target ranked in another of its places than the ranking context is a
neighbour the user may well mean: [[reprioritize X --above A1]], with
A1 one of A's children, says \enquote{rank X among A's children, just
above A1}, whatever X's context is now (\cref{sec:ranking-context}).
So such a target is accepted, and the item is ranked in that place,
through a stand-in whose only parent is the place, as [[add]] and
[[edit]] rank an item in one of its places
(\cref{sec:place-in-places}).  The number found is the item's number
in that place; if another place keeps it higher, the rule lifts it there
when the number is stored.  Only a target in none of the item's places
is not a sibling.

<<rank the item in the place of the target>>=
place = next(
    (
        p for p in parents_of(item)
        if target.id in {t.id for t in ranked_under(todos, p)}
    ),
    None,
)
if place is None:
    typer.echo(
        f"Error: #{target_id} is not a sibling of "
        f"#{todo_id}",
        err=True,
    )
    raise typer.Exit(1)
ranked_as = copy.copy(item)
ranked_as.parents = [place]
@

The last check is the one that is easy to miss.  Being a sibling is
not enough to be \emph{comparable}: the comparison set excludes done
items and other workers' items (\cref{todo:placement}), so a target
outside it has no position in the list we are inserting into.  Left
unchecked, that case would reach the placement helper looking for an
index that is not there.

<<resolve the placement target>>=
target = next(
    (t for t in todos if t.id == target_id), None
)
if target is None:
    typer.echo(
        f"Error: todo #{target_id} not found",
        err=True,
    )
    raise typer.Exit(1)
if target.id == item.id:
    typer.echo(
        f"Error: cannot place #{todo_id} relative to "
        "itself",
        err=True,
    )
    raise typer.Exit(1)
if target.id not in {
    s.id for s in ranking_siblings_of(todos, item)
}:
    <<rank the item in the place of the target>>
if target.priority is None:
    typer.echo(
        f"Error: #{target_id} is unranked; "
        "reprioritize it first",
        err=True,
    )
    raise typer.Exit(1)
if target.id not in [
    s.id for s in comparison_siblings(todos, ranked_as)
]:
    typer.echo(
        f"Error: #{target_id} is not in the comparison "
        f"set for #{todo_id}; done items and other "
        "workers' items are excluded",
        err=True,
    )
    raise typer.Exit(1)
