The claim (\cref{sec:todo-claim}) is the other check that must come
before the worktree.  [[activate_todo_state]] makes the binding one
under the lock, but by then a refused start would already have
created a checkout for an item it may not work on.  The peek has
the stack at hand, so we ask the same question of it first.  If the
peek is stale, nothing worse follows than a refusal that a retry
would not get, or a claim made after the peek, which the locked
check still refuses a moment later.  In that second case the worktree
has been created by then and is left behind; the next start of the
item reuses it, so the cost is an unused checkout, not a wrong one.

