\subsubsection{Settling in the Current Terminal}
\label{todo:start-settle}

When nothing is launched, the task is still started: it is on the
stack and its labels are tracked.  What the shell would have
contributed is the [[cd]] into the working directory and the
[[todo:<id>]] marker in the prompt.  We replace the first with a
line naming the directory---the user is in their own shell and
changes directory themselves, and a resolved worktree is named in
preference to [[wd]] just as the launch would have used it (it has
already been created by [[<<resolve worktree for todo start>>]] and
is left for the user; the post-run cleanup is a property of a run,
and there is none).  The marker is replaced by the tmux context: in
a tracked window the labels were just registered there, so ID-less
[[done]] and [[next]] resolve this task and the shell prompt shows
its chain (\cref{prompt}).

<<settle in the current terminal>>=
settle_wd = worktree_launch or item.wd
if settle_wd:
    typer.echo(f"  Working directory: {settle_wd}")
<<adopt the current window when untracked>>
@

That replacement only holds in a window that \emph{is} tracked.
Registration ([[start_tracking_labels]] with
[[update_tmux_context]]) adds labels to existing pane and window
files and creates none, so in a window the user opened themselves
the task would be active on the stack yet invisible to every
ID-less command run there---the failure a tracked tmux session
turns into \enquote{No active todo} the moment any other window is
tracked.  So when the start lands in an untracked tmux window, we
adopt it (\cref{todo:adopt}): the publication, and the
finalize-on-exit, that [[--window]] would have installed in a
window of its own, installed in the one we are in.  Nothing in
that argument is particular to settling---a blocking direct launch
runs in the same untracked window and adopts it too
(\cref{todo:start-spawn})---so the work is a function shared by the
two paths rather than a chunk reused between them, and the one
place where they differ, the finalize hook, is its parameter.
Headless runs are exempt on both paths; adoption is part of the
interactive workflow, and an agent's window is arranged by whoever
launched it.

One difference from [[adopt]] and [[--window]] is deliberate.
Those publish only the task's own labels, making the window the
task's window.  Here the window is the branch's window: in a
tracked window, [[ensure_ancestors_active]] would already have
registered every ancestor's labels, and the adopted window must end
in the same state.  Otherwise [[done]] on the child would leave the
window with no todo context, and the next [[next]] would jump to
the top level instead of picking a sibling.  The ancestors are the
line [[ensure_ancestors_active]] activated, the [[context_path]] with
the active stack as context: for an item with several parents, the
parent already active is the one the user works under, and its labels,
not the first parent's, belong in the window.  The ancestors were
activated before the window was tracked, so we register them now,
after adoption; the adoption's cleanup hook owns only the task's
labels, and the ancestors leave the window file through [[done]]
and [[stop]] just as they do in a [[--window]] window.

The two [[track]] imports stay inside the function.  Deferring them
keeps [[todo]] usable when [[track]] is missing---the reason every
other call into it is deferred too---and it also keeps each name
resolved through [[nytid.cli.track]] at call time, so the tests can
patch the helpers there rather than having to find a copy bound
into this module at import time.

<<helpers>>=
def adopt_untracked_window_for_start(
    todo_id, item, todos, auto_suspend,
    *, arm_finalize=None,
):
    """Adopt the current tmux window for a starting todo.

    Adopts the window with the task's labels and then registers
    every ancestor's labels on it, so ID-less todo commands run
    there resolve the task and `next` stays inside the branch.
    Does nothing, and returns False, outside tmux or in a window
    that is already tracked.  `arm_finalize` is passed on to
    `adopt_window_for_todo`.
    """
    if not (
        os.environ.get("TMUX")
        and os.environ.get("TMUX_PANE")
    ):
        return False
    from nytid.cli.track import (
        is_current_tmux_context_tracked,
        register_tmux_context_labels,
    )

    worker = session_worker(item)
    if is_current_tmux_context_tracked(worker):
        return False
    adopt_window_for_todo(
        todo_id, item, worker, auto_suspend,
        arm_finalize=arm_finalize,
    )
    for ancestor in context_path(todos, item, load_active_stack()):
        register_tmux_context_labels(
            todo_track_labels(ancestor, ancestor.id),
            worker,
        )
    typer.echo("  Adopted this tmux window")
    return True
