A worktree makes the todo launchable on its own, just as a stored
[[wd]] does; otherwise a todo carrying only a worktree would silently
start tracking without opening the checkout it was meant to run in.

The worktree cleanup (\cref{track:worktrees}) sits after the run and
before [[<<handle subprocess exit>>]] in both blocking arms: the exit
handler may [[return]] early when the item has vanished, and it may
prompt the user, and neither should stop an untouched worktree from
