Todo launches now follow the same context-building path as track launches.
We compute the textual todo context once and reuse it both as the prompt
marker (seeded when we build the shell) and as the tmux window name.  That
keeps direct shells and [[-W]] windows visually consistent.  The
working directory prefers the resolved worktree over the stored [[wd]]:
the worktree was derived from [[wd]] in the first place, so it is the
more specific answer to \enquote{where does this task run?}.

<<prepare subprocess environment>>=
from nytid.cli.track import (
    apply_context_prompt,
    build_context_name,
)

proc_env = os.environ.copy()
if item.env:
    proc_env = dict(item.env)
    <<mirror live session identity into [[proc_env]]>>
todo_context = build_context_name(
    "todo", [str(todo_id)]
