The receipt this prints used to be a line of prose per item,
[[  #12 Fix the parser (issue #340)]], which reads acceptably but is
awkward to scan when a batch import brings in thirty issues: the titles
start at different columns and the issue numbers hide at the end of a
ragged line.
The four pieces of information are really four fields, so we let
[[print_rows]] (\cref{cli.utils.output}) line them up.

The piped bytes therefore change here, from that prose shape to four
tab-separated fields.
That is safe in a way the changes elsewhere in this chapter would not
have been: this is a receipt for an interactive import, not a listing
anything consumes.
No test asserts on its shape --- the import tests check the
[[Imported N items.]] footer and the stored items instead --- and none
of the wrappers we ship parse it.

The footer stays a plain [[typer.echo]].
It is a sentence rather than a row, and it must still appear when
[[committed]] is empty, whereas [[print_rows]] deliberately prints
nothing at all when there is nothing to report.

The skipped items collected by [[<<filter already imported>>]] get the
same treatment as the imported ones: a table of the same four columns,
except that the first column now holds the ID of the local item that
already carries the GitHub number---that ID is the whole point of the
report.  The table is preceded by its own heading line so that a
receipt listing both imported and skipped items does not read as one
long list, and it is followed by a footer of its own for the same
reason the import footer exists: it must still say something when the
table is empty of imports but full of skips.

When the user named one specific item with [[--number]] and it was
skipped, we know exactly what they were trying to achieve---get that
one issue into their list, usually under the current parent---so we
add the one-line hint that does it.  For a batch import without
[[--number]], a long list of skips is the expected steady state of
re-running the import to pick up new issues, and the hint would be
noise.

<<report skipped duplicates>>=
if skipped_items:
    typer.echo("Already imported (skipped):")
    print_rows(
        ["Local", "Title", "Type", "GH #"],
        [
            (
                f"#{local.id}",
                local.title,
                gh_item["_type"],
                f"#{gh_item['number']}",
            )
            for gh_item, local in skipped_items
        ],
    )
    typer.echo(
        f"Skipped {len(skipped_items)} already imported."
    )
    if number is not None:
        local = skipped_items[0][1]
        typer.echo(
            f"Hint: use 'nytid todo edit {local.id} "
            f"--parent <id>' to move it, "
            f"or 'nytid todo show {local.id}' to inspect it."
        )
