GitHub is the authoritative source for issue state: a
collaborator may have closed the issue, or a linked pull request
may have been merged and triggered an auto-close. If GitHub
shows the item as closed but our local copy is still open, we
mark it done locally, with the time GitHub closed it
(\cref{sec:todo-github-closed}), and stop any active time-tracking
session:

<<sync state from github>>=
if (
    gh_state in ("CLOSED", "MERGED")
    and item.status != "done"
):
    set_status(
        item, "done", closed_at=github_time(data, "closedAt"),
    )
    changes += 1
    typer.echo(
        f"  #{item.id} marked done "
        f"(closed on GitHub)"
    )
    stop_todo_tracking(item.id, item, todos)
@

Conversely, if our local item is done but GitHub still shows
it as open, we close it on GitHub:

<<sync state to github>>=
if (
    item.status == "done"
    and gh_state == "OPEN"
):
