\section{Tests}

The test file follows the same pattern as [[track.nw]]: a fixture
provides a temporary directory, and test functions are collected from
throughout the document via chunk concatenation.

Because [[todo start]] and [[todo done]] delegate to the [[track]]
module (\cref{cli.track}), the [[temp_todo_dir]] fixture depends on
[[temp_tracking_dir]] (defined in [[conftest.py]], \cref{conftest})
so that tracking I/O is also redirected into a temporary directory.
Without this, every todo test that starts or stops a task would
write session files into the user's real [[~/.nytid/tracking/]]
directory.

Every test of the module also runs with [[STRICT_RANKING]] set, through
the autouse fixture [[strict_ranking]] defined next to the ranking net
(\cref{sec:ranking-context}), so that a give-up of the repair fails the
test that caused it instead of printing a warning nobody reads.

